hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1518","Issa bin Ibrahim narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, on the authority of Ibn Lahi’ah, and Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Ata’ bin Dinar al-Hudhali: That the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three whose prayers will not be accepted, nor will they ascend to heaven, nor will they go beyond their heads: a man or a people, and they are his own.” Haters, and a man who prayed at a funeral but was not commanded, and a woman whose husband called her in the night but she refused.”"
"1519","On the authority of Issa bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he raises it meaning: like this. Abu Bakr said: I dictated the first part and it is mursal. Because the hadith of Anas, which Jesus narrated after him, means something like it. If it were not for this, I would not have reported the news sent in this book."
